The {{nihongo|'''Nagata Line'''|長田線|Nagata-sen}} is a subway line in [[Okami|Okami (大紙)]], [[Okaiken]], operated by [[Okami Metro]]. It serves as a specialized east-west connector, linking the industrial bay ward of [[Taisho Ward, Okami|Taisho]] with the eastern parklands of [[Tsurumi Ward, Okami|Tsurumi]] and [[Kadoma]]. On system maps, the line is color-coded **lime green** ({{Okami Metro color|N}}), and its stations use the prefix "N".

The Nagata Line was the first subway in Okaiken to utilize **Linear Motor** propulsion. This technology allows the trains to navigate steep grades and sharp curves that conventional trains cannot handle, enabling the line to thread through the densely built-up city center deep underground. The tunnel diameter is significantly smaller than other lines, resulting in compact stations and 4-car trainsets.



==History==
Construction of the Nagata Line began in the 1980s to provide access to the **International Garden and Greenery Exposition (Expo '90)** held at Tsurumi-Ryokuchi. The initial section between [[Kyobashi-Coms Station|Kyobashi-Coms]] and [[Tsurumi-Ryokuchi Station|Tsurumi-Ryokuchi]] opened on March 20, 1990.

The line was subsequently extended westward through the city center, reaching [[Shinsaibashi-Dori Station|Shinsaibashi-Dori]] in 1996 and its current western terminus at [[Taisho-River Station|Taisho-River]] in 1997. This extension created vital cross-town links with every other major subway line in the network.

